('48184b3a-0c14-51f3-9421-eba91502c4c5','bf79c4a8-d119-528a-9335-e5a2d3315589',4,null,null,'written','to feel something with your hand or another part of your body to find out what it is like','[ transitive ]',null,'چیزی را با دست یا قسمت دیگری از بدن خود احساس کنید تا بفهمید که چگونه است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Gingerly she explored the bump on her head with her fingers.","translation":"با نشاط با انگشتانش برآمدگی روی سرش را بررسی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657630.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2d5a37b3-d9ca-576a-b110-1cd83ab88708','80f51ead-0bc8-5b41-8ab0-a65eb407cb40',1,'feeling','احساس','spoken & written','to tell or show what you are feeling or thinking by using words, looks, or actions',null,null,'ابراز کردن، رساندن (فکر، احساس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['express your views/opinions/ideas Everyone who attends the meeting will be given the opportunity to express their opinions.','express your feelings He felt unable to express his feelings in a letter.','express an interest in something Many property developers have expressed an interest in buying the land.','express concern (= say or show that you are worried ) Financial analysts have expressed concern about the possibility of a recession.','express your thanks/gratitude/appreciation (= say thank you to someone, in a speech ) On behalf of the team, I’d like to express our appreciation for all your efforts.','express doubts/reservations (= say or show that you are not sure whether something is true or right ) Environmentalists began to express doubts about the benefits of biofuels.','express surprise/shock ‘I don’t believe he could hurt anyone, ’ she said, expressing her surprise.','express anger Teachers have expressed anger at the government’s education reforms.','express your grief (= say or show that you are very sad, especially because someone you love has died ) She searched for further words to express her grief, but could find none.','express your sympathy (= say that you feel sorry for someone who is in a bad situation ) I wrote to his widow expressing our sympathy and sending her our condolences.','express confidence Throughout the trial, his legal team expressed confidence in the outcome.','express your hopes/desires (= say what you hope or want to happen ) Nadia expressed her hopes about remaining in San Diego County with her two children.','express your support (= say that you support someone or something ) The Israeli leader expressed his support for the U.S. plan.','express opposition to something (= say that you oppose someone or something ) Local people have expressed their opposition to plans for a new airport.','express a willingness to do something (= say or show that you are willing to do something ) The unions expressed a willingness to have talks with the employers.','express something openly (= express a feeling in a way that is obvious to other people ) They expressed their anger openly in the meeting.','express something clearly (= express an idea or opinion in a way that other people can understand ) He expresses his views very clearly.','express yourself (= say what you think or feel ) He is very confident and finds it easy to express himself.','a chance/opportunity to express something The debate will give MPs an opportunity to express their views in detail.','words cannot express something (= it is impossible to describe something ) Words can’t express how much I miss her.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Bill’s not afraid to express his opinions.","translation":"بیل از بیان نظرات خود نمی ترسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199641.mp3"},{"sentence":"Parents have expressed their concerns about their children’s safety.","translation":"والدین نگرانی های خود را در مورد امنیت فرزندانشان بیان کرده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199644.mp3"},{"sentence":"She expressed an interest in seeing York.","translation":"او به دیدن یورک ابراز علاقه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657768.mp3"},{"sentence":"Express your reasons for applying in simple terms.","translation":"دلایل خود را برای درخواست به زبان ساده بیان کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657776.mp3"},{"sentence":"She doesn’t express her emotions as much as he does.","translation":"او احساسات خود را به اندازه او ابراز نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657777.mp3"},{"sentence":"Finally, I’d like to express my sincere thanks to all those who have helped today.","translation":"در پایان، من می خواهم صمیمانه تشکر کنم از همه کسانی که امروز کمک کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199656.mp3"},{"sentence":"The USA expressed reservations before agreeing to sign the agreement.","translation":"ایالات متحده قبل از موافقت با امضای این توافق نامه ابراز نگرانی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657780.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many people have expressed their opposition to the proposals.","translation":"بسیاری از مردم مخالفت خود را با این پیشنهادات اعلام کرده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657781.mp3"},{"sentence":"Young children often have difficulty expressing themselves.","translation":"کودکان خردسال اغلب در بیان خود مشکل دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199660.mp3"},{"sentence":"He first learnt to express himself through movement at his dance classes.","translation":"او اولین بار در کلاس های رقص خود یاد گرفت که خود را از طریق حرکت بیان کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657787.mp3"},{"sentence":"Words can’t express (= it is impossible to describe ) how angry we felt.","translation":"کلمات نمی توانند بیان کنند (= توصیف غیرممکن است) چقدر عصبانی بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199663.mp3"}]'::jsonb,11),
