 say that you oppose someone or something ) Local people have expressed their opposition to plans for a new airport.','express a willingness to do something (= say or show that you are willing to do something ) The unions expressed a willingness to have talks with the employers.','express something openly (= express a feeling in a way that is obvious to other people ) They expressed their anger openly in the meeting.','express something clearly (= express an idea or opinion in a way that other people can understand ) He expresses his views very clearly.','express yourself (= say what you think or feel ) He is very confident and finds it easy to express himself.','a chance/opportunity to express something The debate will give MPs an opportunity to express their views in detail.','words cannot express something (= it is impossible to describe something ) Words can’t express how much I miss her.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Many of Munch’s paintings express a deep feeling of despair.","translation":"بسیاری از نقاشی های مونک بیانگر احساس عمیق ناامیدی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001199668.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
