('bdc70e0f-147d-5f4e-9afa-94b63268774b','c74cb864-220d-5565-80c5-2a3a4fb03abb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation, quality etc which is as great as it can possibly be – used especially when talking about two opposites',null,null,'یک موقعیت، کیفیت و غیره که تا حد ممکن عالی است - مخصوصاً وقتی در مورد دو متضاد صحبت می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The bacteria can withstand extremes of heat and cold.","translation":"این باکتری می تواند در برابر گرما و سرما مقاومت کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627657.mp3"},{"sentence":"In fact, the truth lies between the two extremes .","translation":"در واقع، حقیقت بین دو افراط نهفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627658.mp3"},{"sentence":"At the other extreme is a country like Switzerland with almost no unemployment.","translation":"در نقطه مقابل کشوری مانند سوئیس قرار دارد که تقریباً هیچ بیکاری ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627664.mp3"},{"sentence":"Advertisements seem to go from one extreme to the other (= change from one extreme thing to something totally opposite ) .","translation":"به نظر می رسد تبلیغات از یک افراط به دیگری می رود (= تغییر از یک چیز افراطی به چیزی کاملاً مخالف).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001627665.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('8848a881-0b02-5e88-903a-6d50b5607a34','c74cb864-220d-5565-80c5-2a3a4fb03abb',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in the extreme',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1cbe1997-cb02-5749-ace6-c915cfd9e1bf','c74cb864-220d-5565-80c5-2a3a4fb03abb',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'to extremes',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('a66554e5-6b4a-5cf3-9f91-3c2ebea96777','7465efbd-a4f1-5740-8260-24b2d71e8f1e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a building or group of buildings in which goods are produced in large quantities , using machines',null,null,'کارخانه، کارگاه صنعتی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a car/textile/shoe etc factory There is a large car factory where many of the local people work.','a factory worker The factory workers are threatening to go on strike.','a factory owner The factory owner placed a large order for some new equipment.','a factory manager He held the position of factory manager.','a factory inspector (= an official whose job is to check that laws or rules related to factories are being obeyed ) Factory inspectors reported that safety precautions had been ignored.','the factory gates (= the entrance to a factory ) A crowd of protesters had gathered outside the factory gates.','open a factory The company has just opened a new factory in Swindon.','close/shut (down) a factory The factory was closed down in 2006.','work in a factory Donna works in a shoe factory.','a factory produces/makes something The factory produces an incredible 100 cars per hour.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a car factory","translation":"یک کارخانه ماشین سازی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206840.mp3"},{"sentence":"factory workers","translation":"کارگران کارخانه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001206841.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8fe750ee-22e1-5f42-8e13-9edf68a1a8f8','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',1,'lack of success','عدم موفقیت','spoken & written','a lack of success in achieving or doing something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'شکست، ناکامی؛ کوتاهی؛ خرابی (موتور)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['end in/result in failure A series of rescue attempts ended in failure.','be doomed to failure (= be certain to fail ) The rebellion was doomed to failure from the start.','admit failure He was too proud to admit failure.','accept failure Being able to accept failure is part of life.','avoid failure She was anxious to avoid failure.','complete/total/utter failure The project ended in total failure.','abject/dismal failure (= used to emphasize how bad a failure is ) The experiment was considered a dismal failure.','a personal failure (= a failure that is someone''s personal fault ) He considered his inability to form long-term relationships to be a personal failure.','economic failure Economic failure drove the government out of office.','fear of failure Fear of failure should not deter you from trying.','the risk/possibility of failure The risk of failure for a new product is very high. The possibility of failure was sufficiently high for the auditors to warn investors.','an admission of failure Dropping out of college would be an admission of failure.','a history of failure (= a situation in which someone has failed many times in the past ) Some children have a history of failure at school.','a string of failures (= a series of failures ) The team has had a string of failures in recent games.','a sense of failure People may feel a sense of failure if they admit they have ended up in a job they hate.','the consequences of failure The political consequences of failure would be defeat at the next election.','a failure rate There is a high failure rate in the restaurant industry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Successful people often aren’t very good at dealing with failure.","translation":"افراد موفق اغلب در مقابله با شکست خیلی خوب نیستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000555.mp3"},{"sentence":"the conference’s failure to reach an agreement","translation":"ناکامی کنفرانس در دستیابی به توافق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638380.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c44d07bb-42d7-552f-9379-faa68170a2f2','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',2,'unsuccessful person/thing','شخص / چیز ناموفق','spoken & written','someone or something that is not successful','[ countable ]',null,'کسی یا چیزی که موفق نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['end in/result in failure A series of rescue attempts ended in failure.','be doomed to failure (= be certain to fail ) The rebellion was doomed to failure from the start.','admit failure He was too proud to admit failure.','accept failure Being able to accept failure is part of life.','avoid failure She was anxious to avoid failure.','complete/total/utter failure The project ended in total failure.','abject/dismal failure (= used to emphasize how bad a failure is ) The experiment was considered a dismal failure.','a personal failure (= a failure that is someone''s personal fault ) He considered his inability to form long-term relationships to be a personal failure.','economic failure Economic failure drove the government out of office.','fear of failure Fear of failure should not deter you from trying.','the risk/possibility of failure The risk of failure for a new product is very high. The possibility of failure was sufficiently high for the auditors to warn investors.','an admission of failure Dropping out of college would be an admission of failure.','a history of failure (= a situation in which someone has failed many times in the past ) Some children have a history of failure at school.','a string of failures (= a series of failures ) The team has had a string of failures in recent games.','a sense of failure People may feel a sense of failure if they admit they have ended up in a job they hate.','the consequences of failure The political consequences of failure would be defeat at the next election.','a failure rate There is a high failure rate in the restaurant industry.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I always felt a bit of a failure at school.","translation":"من همیشه در مدرسه کمی احساس شکست داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001208754.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a7609d7b-d965-5a5e-b52d-b90d0fdcbd63','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'failure to do something','شکست، ناکامی؛ کوتاهی؛ خرابی (موتور)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('acd9edf1-d662-5c9d-843f-add75b9d586d','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',4,'business','کسب و کار','spoken & written','a situation in which a business has to close because of a lack of money','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'وضعیتی که در آن یک کسب و کار به دلیل کمبود پول باید تعطیل شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Business failures in Scotland rose 10% last year.","translation":"شکست های تجاری در اسکاتلند در سال گذشته 10 درصد افزایش یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001208785.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('017be9e7-aae9-59c0-9e21-96def585af85','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',5,'machine/body part','دستگاه/قسمت بدن','spoken & written','an occasion when a machine or part of your body stops working properly','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که دستگاه یا بخشی از بدن شما به درستی کار نمی کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The cause of the crash was engine failure.","translation":"علت تصادف خرابی موتور اعلام شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001208772.mp3"},{"sentence":"He died from kidney failure.","translation":"او بر اثر نارسایی کلیه درگذشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638383.mp3"},{"sentence":"a failure in the computer system","translation":"نقص در سیستم کامپیوتری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001208775.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('a0ef08e1-0b6f-54a6-9e8d-38bb842b8ee4','bb0d3afb-c742-51e9-99b7-2ad022d52908',6,'crops','محصولات زراعی','spoken & written','an occasion when crops do not grow or produce food, for example because of bad weather','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که محصولات رشد نمی کنند یا غذا تولید نمی کنند، برای مثال به دلیل آب و هوای بد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a series of crop failures","translation":"یک سری شکست محصول","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001638389.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e0f5a5b2-26e4-501b-aa05-606ec843ccdd','86ed13e5-2b0b-5f4d-bfcd-366b6bcb380b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is popular or thought to be good at a particular time','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مد، رواج؛ شیوه، سبک','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in fashion Belted jackets are in fashion this winter.','be out of fashion Flared trousers were out of fashion in the 1980s.','go out of fashion (= stop being fashionable ) Long evening dresses are going out of fashion.','come back into fashion (= become fashionable again ) Short skirts are coming back into fashion this year.','be the height of fashion (= be very fashionable ) With her short dress and high boots she was the height of fashion.','keep up with fashion (= make sure that you know about the most recent fashions ) Lucy likes to keep up with the latest fashions.','fashion-conscious (= very interested in the latest fashions, and always wanting to wear fashionable clothes ) Fashion-conscious people can’t get enough of these new designs.','the latest fashion They sell all the latest fashions.','men’s/women’s fashions Men’s fashions have not changed much in 50 years.','the fashion industry London is the centre of the British fashion industry.','the fashion world Small women are often overlooked by the fashion world.','a fashion show Calvin Klein’s fashion show featured suits and sportswear.','a fashion model Fashion models are usually very tall.','a fashion designer Her favourite fashion designers include Giorgio Armani and Gianfranco Ferre.','fashion design He went to St Martin’s School of Art to study fashion design.','a fashion house (= a company that produces new and expensive styles of clothes ) fashion houses such as Armani and Hugo Boss','a fashion magazine She’s the editor of a leading fashion magazine.','fashion photography a book of Lang’s fashion photography','a fashion photographer Later he worked as a fashion photographer for Vogue.','a fashion shoot (= an occasion when photographs are taken of fashion models ) She was asked to star with top model Naomi Campbell in a fashion shoot.','a fashion shop We walked around Milan’s famous fashion shops.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the fashion for ‘discovery methods’ of learning","translation":"مد برای \"روش های کشف\" یادگیری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001641896.mp3"},{"sentence":"The emerging science of photography was already changing fashions in art.","translation":"علم نوظهور عکاسی در حال تغییر مد در هنر بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985903.mp3"},{"sentence":"Bright colours are in fashion this summer.","translation":"رنگ های روشن در این تابستان مد هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00328.mp3"},{"sentence":"Their music will never go out of fashion.","translation":"موسیقی آنها هرگز از مد نمی افتد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985909.mp3"},{"sentence":"His ideas are coming back into fashion (= they are becoming popular again ) .","translation":"ایده های او دوباره به مد می آیند (= دوباره محبوب می شوند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001641897.mp3"},{"sentence":"Eastern religions used to be the fashion in the 60s.","translation":"مذاهب شرقی در دهه 60 مد بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985904.mp3"},{"sentence":"Self-help books are all the fashion (= they are very fashionable ) .","translation":"کتاب های خودیاری همه مد هستند (= خیلی مد هستند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985914.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('74aefafe-9c75-52fb-819b-84f485920444','86ed13e5-2b0b-5f4d-bfcd-366b6bcb380b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a style of clothes , hair etc that is popular at a particular time','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک مدل لباس، مو و غیره که در یک زمان خاص محبوب است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in fashion Belted jackets are in fashion this winter.','be out of fashion Flared trousers were out of fashion in the 1980s.','go out of fashion (= stop being fashionable ) Long evening dresses are going out of fashion.','come back into fashion (= become fashionable again ) Short skirts are coming back into fashion this year.','be the height of fashion (= be very fashionable ) With her short dress and high boots she was the height of fashion.','keep up with fashion (= make sure that you know about the most recent fashions ) Lucy likes to keep up with the latest fashions.','fashion-conscious (= very interested in the latest fashions, and always wanting to wear fashionable clothes ) Fashion-conscious people can’t get enough of these new designs.','the latest fashion They sell all the latest fashions.','men’s/women’s fashions Men’s fashions have not changed much in 50 years.','the fashion industry London is the centre of the British fashion industry.','the fashion world Small women are often overlooked by the fashion world.','a fashion show Calvin Klein’s fashion show featured suits and sportswear.','a fashion model Fashion models are usually very tall.','a fashion designer Her favourite fashion designers include Giorgio Armani and Gianfranco Ferre.','fashion design He went to St Martin’s School of Art to study fashion design.','a fashion house (= a company that produces new and expensive styles of clothes ) fashion houses such as Armani and Hugo Boss','a fashion magazine She’s the editor of a leading fashion magazine.','fashion photography a book of Lang’s fashion photography','a fashion photographer Later he worked as a fashion photographer for Vogue.','a fashion shoot (= an occasion when photographs are taken of fashion models ) She was asked to star with top model Naomi Campbell in a fashion shoot.','a fashion shop We walked around Milan’s famous fashion shops.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Young people are very concerned with fashion.","translation":"جوانان علاقه زیادی به مد دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000563.mp3"},{"sentence":"The store has all the latest fashions.","translation":"فروشگاه دارای آخرین مدهای روز است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00329.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('700745bf-d6bc-553c-9254-c9197e27e80f','86ed13e5-2b0b-5f4d-bfcd-366b6bcb380b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the business or study of making and selling clothes, shoes etc in new and changing styles','[ uncountable ]',null,'کسب و کار یا مطالعه ساخت و فروش لباس، کفش و غیره به سبک های جدید و در حال تغییر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be in fashion Belted jackets are in fashion this winter.','be out of fashion Flared trousers were out of fashion in the 1980s.','go out of fashion (= stop being fashionable ) Long evening dresses are going out of fashion.','come back into fashion (= become fashionable again ) Short skirts are coming back into fashion this year.','be the height of fashion (= be very fashionable ) With her short dress and high boots she was the height of fashion.','keep up with fashion (= make sure that you know about the most recent fashions ) Lucy likes to keep up with the latest fashions.','fashion-conscious (= very interested in the latest fashions, and always wanting to wear fashionable clothes ) Fashion-conscious people can’t get enough of these new designs.','the latest fashion They sell all the latest fashions.','men’s/women’s fashions Men’s fashions have not changed much in 50 years.','the fashion industry London is the centre of the British fashion industry.','the fashion world Small women are often overlooked by the fashion world.','a fashion show Calvin Klein’s fashion show featured suits and sportswear.','a fashion model Fashion models are usually very tall.','a fashion designer Her favourite fashion designers include Giorgio Armani and Gianfranco Ferre.','fashion design He went to St Martin’s School of Art to study fashion design.','a fashion house (= a company that produces new and expensive styles of clothes ) fashion houses such as Armani and Hugo Boss','a fashion magazine She’s the editor of a leading fashion magazine.','fashion photography a book of Lang’s fashion photography','a fashion photographer Later he worked as a fashion pho