('e179e84b-4343-5919-aa96-ba5ed5545c12','97f646d6-0a03-5e24-8714-e19a6cfeda24',6,null,null,'spoken & written','a fixed and familiar series of words that seems meaningless or insincere','[ countable ]',null,'یک سری کلمات ثابت و آشنا که بی معنی یا غیر صادقانه به نظر می رسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a speech full of the usual formulas and clichés","translation":"سخنرانی پر از فرمول ها و کلیشه های معمول","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001274166.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6f45e152-2567-5c71-b4ab-e056cfd76580','867e460c-92a9-5636-80bd-33031f125d8c',1,'money','پول','spoken & written','a very large amount of money','[ countable ]',null,'ثروت، گنج؛ سرنوشت، اقبال','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a fortune ( also amass a fortune formal ) (= gain a lot of money ) His family amassed a fortune during that period.','make your fortune (= become rich ) She made her fortune in the cosmetics industry.','earn a fortune He hopes to earn a fortune from his latest invention.','lose a fortune (= lose a lot of money ) He lost a fortune in an unwise business deal.','cost a fortune (= be very expensive ) It’ll cost a fortune if we go by taxi.','spend a fortune You don’t have to spend a fortune giving your family healthy meals.','pay a fortune (= pay a lot of money ) We had to pay a fortune in rent.','inherit a fortune (= gain a lot of money after someone dies ) He inherited a fortune of a million pounds from his uncle.','leave somebody a fortune (= arrange for someone to receive a lot of money after you die ) He left his wife a modest fortune.','a huge/vast/immense fortune Timothy was the heir to a vast fortune.','a large/substantial/considerable fortune His father, an oil magnate, amassed a large fortune.','a small fortune (= a very large amount of money ) He made a small fortune in the London property boom.','a personal/private fortune She is one of the richest women in Britain, with an estimated personal fortune of £90 million.','a £20 million/$40 million etc fortune She is believed to have a £25 million fortune.','be worth a fortune informal: The building itself is worth a fortune.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He made a fortune selling property in Spain.","translation":"او با فروش ملک در اسپانیا ثروت زیادی به دست آورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731163.mp3"},{"sentence":"My first painting sold for £25, a small fortune then for an art student.","translation":"اولین نقاشی من به قیمت 25 پوند فروخته شد که در آن زمان برای یک دانشجوی هنر ثروت اندکی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731167.mp3"},{"sentence":"He died in poverty in 1947, but his art is worth a fortune .","translation":"او در سال 1947 در فقر درگذشت، اما هنر او ارزش یک ثروت را دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731171.mp3"},{"sentence":"The carpet must have cost a fortune .","translation":"فرش باید گران تمام شده باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731175.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is quite easy to decorate your house without spending a fortune .","translation":"تزئین خانه بدون صرف هزینه بسیار آسان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731179.mp3"},{"sentence":"Her personal fortune was estimated at £37 million.","translation":"ثروت شخصی او 37 میلیون پوند تخمین زده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731183.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('4dd72f68-f01b-5e47-a8f8-82f1f78936fc','867e460c-92a9-5636-80bd-33031f125d8c',2,'chance','شانس','spoken & written','chance or luck , and the effect that it has on your life','[ uncountable ]',null,'شانس یا شانس و تأثیری که بر زندگی شما می گذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make a fortune ( also amass a fortune formal ) (= gain a lot of money ) His family amassed a fortune during that period.','make your fortune (= become rich ) She made her fortune in the cosmetics industry.','earn a fortune He hopes to earn a fortune from his latest invention.','lose a fortune (= lose a lot of money ) He lost a fortune in an unwise business deal.','cost a fortune (= be very expensive ) It’ll cost a fortune if we go by taxi.','spend a fortune You don’t have to spend a fortune giving your family healthy meals.','pay a fortune (= pay a lot of money ) We had to pay a fortune in rent.','inherit a fortune (= gain a lot of money after someone dies ) He inherited a fortune of a million pounds from his uncle.','leave somebody a fortune (= arrange for someone to receive a lot of money after you die ) He left his wife a modest fortune.','a huge/vast/immense fortune Timothy was the heir to a vast fortune.','a large/substantial/considerable fortune His father, an oil magnate, amassed a large fortune.','a small fortune (= a very large amount of money ) He made a small fortune in the London property boom.','a personal/private fortune She is one of the richest women in Britain, with an estimated personal fortune of £90 million.','a £20 million/$40 million etc fortune She is believed to have a £25 million fortune.','be worth a fortune informal: The building itself is worth a fortune.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I had the good fortune to work with a brilliant head of department.","translation":"من این شانس را داشتم که با یک رئیس دپارتمان باهوش کار کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731187.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sickness or ill fortune could reduce you to a needy situation.","translation":"بیماری یا بدبختی می تواند شما را به یک وضعیت نیازمند برساند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731191.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt it was useless to struggle against fortune.","translation":"احساس کردم مبارزه با ثروت بی فایده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001274656.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
