('c836ade1-2c31-5fcf-9a8b-3e30ae41e2bb','a704769e-2e18-5476-93d5-a006827d4850',5,null,null,'formal','too confident and friendly in dealing with people you do not know very well',null,null,'بیش از حد اعتماد به نفس و دوستانه در برخورد با افرادی که به خوبی نمی شناسید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"My father thinks she’s far too forward for a young girl.","translation":"پدرم فکر می‌کند که او برای یک دختر جوان خیلی جلوگیر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731237.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ee00f5d1-598c-537e-90ab-1fb0bc74c272','f25ac70e-e683-5166-80ad-0f5c8133759d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to send letters, goods etc to someone when they have moved to a different address',null,null,'برای ارسال نامه ها، کالاها و غیره برای کسی که به آدرس دیگری نقل مکان کرده است',array['send on']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Would you make sure that you forward my mail promptly?","translation":"آیا مطمئن می شوید که نامه من را فورا فوروارد می کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001731239.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7c2048bb-4225-5c43-a680-984d2d9a283e','f25ac70e-e683-5166-80ad-0f5c8133759d',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to send letters, information etc to someone',null,null,'برای ارسال نامه، اطلاعات و غیره به کسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Flight times will be forwarded to you with your travel documentation.","translation":"زمان پرواز همراه با مدارک سفر برای شما ارسال می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001274903.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a7bd305b-ff70-5077-a70a-df08867be219','f25ac70e-e683-5166-80ad-0f5c8133759d',3,null,null,'formal','to help something to develop so that it becomes successful',null,null,'کمک کردن به چیزی برای توسعه به طوری که موفق شود',array['further']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a good chance to forward my career","translation":"فرصت خوبی برای پیشرفت حرفه ای ام","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001274912.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('83b8faf4-7d27-5cde-97c4-d07458e5e5cb','d9b6fc5b-7949-5ade-b7fa-2f5a83fabbe3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an attacking player on a team in sports such as football and basketball',null,null,'بازیکن مهاجم در یک تیم در ورزش هایی مانند فوتبال و بسکتبال','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0a85d0d8-311c-5d6a-88ac-6447c8cad512','6e1c918d-1db7-5ef8-afc5-2ba695bd515f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to show that you are saying what you really think about something',null,null,'رک و راست، صادقانه (حرف زدن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Frankly, I think the Internet is overrated.","translation":"صادقانه بگویم، من فکر می کنم اینترنت بیش از حد ارزیابی شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001277383.mp3"},{"sentence":"His behaviour was frankly disgraceful.","translation":"رفتار او صراحتا شرم آور بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700044.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('49c2cb32-a0bc-5391-a424-cec4626e13b5','6e1c918d-1db7-5ef8-afc5-2ba695bd515f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','honestly and directly',null,null,'صادقانه و مستقیم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She answered all our questions frankly.","translation":"او با صراحت به تمام سوالات ما پاسخ داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700045.mp3"},{"sentence":"Nicholas frankly admitted that the report was a pack of lies.","translation":"نیکلاس صریحاً اعتراف کرد که این گزارش مجموعه ای از دروغ بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001277378.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9c58fad9-a3a1-50cf-9140-78435438e197','a3df2c1e-07a4-5d26-8e11-ca9de19fd84f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the right to do what you want without being controlled or restricted by anyone','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'آزادی؛ استقلال (دسترسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['total/complete freedom Riding a motorbike gives me a feeling of total freedom.','great/considerable freedom Teachers are given considerable freedom to choose their teaching methods.','personal/individual freedom Our personal freedom is being restricted more and more.','political/religious freedom (= freedom to have any political/religious beliefs ) The people were given political freedom for the first time in the country''s history.','academic freedom (= freedom to teach or study any ideas ) She refused, on the grounds of academic freedom, to amend the course.','artistic freedom (= freedom to create anything as an artist ) Banning the film would be an unacceptable restriction on artistic freedom.','have the freedom to do something We have the freedom to travel nearly anywhere in the world.','enjoy freedom Filmmakers today enjoy more freedom than in the past.','the struggle/fight for freedom The student movement played an important role in the struggle for political freedom.','freedom of speech/expression (= the legal right to say what you want ) We will defend freedom of speech and oppose censorship.','freedom of religion/worship (= the right to hold/practise any religious belief ) Liberal newspapers made an effort to secure religious toleration and freedom of worship.','freedom of movement (= the right or ability to travel, or the ability to move your body freely ) Thanks to the automobile, Americans had a previously unknown freedom of movement. The tight uniforms restrict their freedom of movement.','freedom of assembly (= the right of people to meet as a group for a particular purpose ) Restrictions on freedom of assembly were gradually relaxed.','the freedom of the press (= the right of newspapers to publish what they like, free from political control ) The freedom of the press is written into the country''s constitution.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"People here like their freedom and privacy.","translation":"مردم اینجا آزادی و حریم خصوصی خود را دوست دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700162.mp3"},{"sentence":"the rights and freedoms of citizens","translation":"حقوق و آزادی های شهروندان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001280088.mp3"},{"sentence":"We do not have the freedom to do just what we like.","translation":"ما آزادی انجام کاری را که دوست داریم نداریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001824261.mp3"},{"sentence":"the freedom to vote","translation":"آزادی رای دادن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700165.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tighter security measures are restricting our freedom of movement (= the right to travel ) .","translation":"تدابیر امنیتی شدیدتر آزادی حرکت ما (= حق سفر) را محدود می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000626.mp3"},{"sentence":"The First Amendment guarantees freedom of expression .","translation":"متمم اول آزادی بیان را تضمین می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001280092.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('22f6a093-e1f2-5422-be72-1ee79ec42aba','a3df2c1e-07a4-5d26-8e11-ca9de19fd84f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the state of being free and allowed to do what you want','[ uncountable ]',null,'حالت آزاد بودن و اجازه انجام کاری که می خواهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['total/complete freedom Riding a motorbike gives me a feeling of total freedom.','great/considerable freedom Teachers are given considerable freedom to choose their teaching methods.','personal/individual freedom Our personal freedom is being restricted more and more.','political/religious freedom (= freedom to have any political/religious beliefs ) The people were given political freedom for the first time in the country''s history.','academic freedom (= freedom to teach or study any ideas ) She refused, on the grounds of academic freedom, to amend the course.','artistic freedom (= freedom to create anything as an artist ) Banning the film would be an unacceptable restriction on artistic freedom.','have the freedom to do something We have the freedom to travel nearly anywhere in the world.','enjoy freedom Filmmakers today enjoy more freedom than in the past.','the struggle/fight for freedom The student movement played an important role in the struggle for political freedom.','freedom of speech/expression (= the legal right to say what you want ) We will defend freedom of speech and oppose censorship.','freedom of religion/worship (= the right to hold/practise any religious belief ) Liberal newspapers made an effort to secure religious toleration and freedom of worship.','freedom of movement (= the right or ability to travel, or the ability to move your body freely ) Thanks to the automobile, Americans had a previously unknown freedom of movement. The tight uniforms restrict their freedom of movement.','freedom of assembly (= the right of people to meet as a group for a particular purpose ) Restrictions on freedom of assembly were gradually relaxed.','the freedom of the press (= the right of newspapers to publish what they like, free from political control ) The freedom of the press is written into the country''s constitution.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He thinks children have too much freedom these days.","translation":"او فکر می کند این روزها بچه ها آزادی زیادی دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000627.mp3"},{"sentence":"The wheelchair gives him the freedom to go out on his own.","translation":"ویلچر به او این آزادی را می دهد که خودش بیرون برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700176.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tracksuits are designed to give you freedom of movement (= the ability to move your body freely ) .","translation":"لباس‌های ورزشی به گونه‌ای طراحی شده‌اند که به شما آزادی حرکت (= توانایی حرکت آزادانه بدنتان) بدهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001700177.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('4af5ea80-d18f-57bf-9967-5ab94c657c73','a3df2c1e-07a4-5d26-8e11-ca9de19fd84f',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the state of being free because you are not in prison','[ uncountable ]',null,'وضعیت آزادی چون در زندان نیستی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The prisoner was recaptured after only 48 hours of freedom.","translation":"این زندانی تنها پس از 48 ساعت آزادی دوباره دستگیر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001280108.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
