('368ec009-b5f9-59f4-a137-e998e9dda52e','ffbbca8d-3e7d-5a41-adf0-ab5211f24174',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the sense which you use to hear sounds','[ uncountable ]','hard of hearing','شنوایی، حس شنیدن؛ نشست (دادگاه)؛ جلسه رسیدگی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have good/bad etc hearing Dogs have excellent hearing.','lose your hearing (= become unable to hear ) He lost his hearing as a child after suffering scarlet fever.','affect/impair your hearing (= make your hearing worse ) Listening to loud music will eventually impair your hearing.','somebody''s hearing gets worse ( also somebody''s hearing deteriorates ) The medication seemed to make her hearing get worse.','somebody''s hearing goes (= someone becomes unable to hear ) His hearing has gone in one ear.','good/sharp/acute My hearing isn''t as good as it used to be. Owls and other predatory birds have very acute hearing.','bad/poor Poor hearing can affect your social relationships.','impaired (= having problems with hearing ) There are about 11,000 people in the UK whose sight and hearing are both severely impaired.','normal He was born with normal hearing but became deaf at the age of 11.','hearing loss Many older people suffer from some degree of hearing loss.','a hearing problem/difficulty/impairment a special telephone for people with hearing problems','be hard of hearing (= not be able to hear well ) The subtitling service is intended for people who are hard of hearing.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has remarkable hearing for a lady of her age.","translation":"او شنوایی قابل توجهی برای یک خانم هم سن و سال خود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001350984.mp3"},{"sentence":"a child with a hearing disability","translation":"کودکی با ناتوانی شنوایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001757825.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
