('29e58c4a-b806-5066-9e63-14667dd8df30','11dd4704-6595-530b-8ade-ff1389599885',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a long talk on a particular subject that someone gives to a group of people, especially to students in a university',null,null,'سخنرانی، درس‌گفتار؛ موعظه (کوبنده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give a lecture ( also deliver a lecture formal ) She gave a fascinating lecture on crime in the 1800s. He delivered the lecture at the London School of Economics.','do a lecture informal: He’s doing a lecture on modern poetry.','go to a lecture ( also attend a lecture formal ) Have you been to any of Professor MacPherson’s lectures? I recently attended a lecture by a noted historian.','listen to a lecture Most students spend about a quarter of their time listening to lectures.','a lecture hall/room ( also a lecture theatre British English ) The lecture hall was packed.','lecture notes Can I borrow your lecture notes?','a lecture tour (= a trip that someone takes to many different places to give a lecture ) He’s on a lecture tour of the US.','a series of lectures ( also a course of lectures British English ) a series of lectures on the history of art','a public lecture (= a lecture which the general public are allowed to go to ) He’s going to deliver a public lecture on politics in the Middle East.','an illustrated lecture (= a lecture with pictures such as slides ) Mrs Robinson gave a fascinating illustrated lecture on Spanish history.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He regularly gives lectures on modern French literature.","translation":"او مرتباً در مورد ادبیات مدرن فرانسه سخنرانی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001493732.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7ca1142f-cd85-52c0-9d94-c818a73e3b18','11dd4704-6595-530b-8ade-ff1389599885',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an act of criticizing someone or warning them about something in a long serious talk, in a way that they think is unfair or unnecessary',null,null,'عمل انتقاد از کسی یا هشدار دادن به او در مورد چیزی در یک سخنرانی طولانی و جدی، به گونه ای که فکر می کند غیرمنصفانه یا غیر ضروری است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give a lecture ( also deliver a lecture formal ) She gave a fascinating lecture on crime in the 1800s. He delivered the lecture at the London School of Economics.','do a lecture informal: He’s doing a lecture on modern poetry.','go to a lecture ( also attend a lecture formal ) Have you been to any of Professor MacPherson’s lectures? I recently attended a lecture by a noted historian.','listen to a lecture Most students spend about a quarter of their time listening to lectures.','a lecture hall/room ( also a lecture theatre British English ) The lecture hall was packed.','lecture notes Can I borrow your lecture notes?','a lecture tour (= a trip that someone takes to many different places to give a lecture ) He’s on a lecture tour of the US.','a series of lectures ( also a course of lectures British English ) a series of lectures on the history of art','a public lecture (= a lecture which the general public are allowed to go to ) He’s going to deliver a public lecture on politics in the Middle East.','an illustrated lecture (= a lecture with pictures such as slides ) Mrs Robinson gave a fascinating illustrated lecture on Spanish history.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"My father caught me and gave me a long lecture about the dangers of drink.","translation":"پدرم مرا گرفت و یک سخنرانی طولانی درباره مضرات نوشیدنی به من داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001493738.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a3e96477-8cee-5899-9a94-18b5a6b095f9','a99b77d7-4ebb-5264-9c09-c710c7f78aba',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to talk angrily or seriously to someone in order to criticize or warn them, in a way that they think is unfair or unnecessary','[ transitive ]',null,'با عصبانیت یا جدی صحبت کردن با کسی به منظور انتقاد یا هشدار دادن به او به گونه ای که فکر می کند ناعادلانه یا غیر ضروری است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I wish you’d stop lecturing me!","translation":"ای کاش دیگر به من سخنرانی نمی کردی!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001493748.mp3"},{"sentence":"He began to lecture us about making too much noise.","translation":"او شروع به سخنرانی در مورد سر و صدای زیاد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749039.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b1adcb1c-aa47-53c4-be0d-0effd58caa39','a99b77d7-4ebb-5264-9c09-c710c7f78aba',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to talk to a group of people on a particular subject, especially to students in a university','[ intransitive ]',null,'صحبت کردن با گروهی از افراد در مورد یک موضوع خاص، به ویژه با دانشجویان یک دانشگاه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He lectures on European art at Manchester University.","translation":"او در دانشگاه منچستر در مورد هنر اروپا سخنرانی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749042.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('35c00454-68f6-5f1f-b45d-ce041897a977','3e66efae-90d9-5081-8379-91a03acb7269',1,null,null,'spoken & written','time when you are not working or studying and can relax and do things you enjoy',null,null,'فراغت، اوقات فراغت؛ آسودگی (وضع)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['leisure time They spend much of their leisure time with their grandchildren.','a leisure activity/interest Many people have little time after work for leisure activities.','leisure pursuits formal (= leisure activities ) Ask about his hobbies and leisure pursuits.','a leisure centre/complex (= a place where you can play sports etc ) The local leisure centre has a swimming pool and a sauna.','leisure facilities (= different places where you can play sports etc ) The leisure facilities in the town are very good.','the leisure industry/sector The leisure sector has experienced phenomenal growth in recent years.','a leisure group (= a group of companies in the leisure industry ) The leisure group reported record profits last year.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most people now enjoy shorter working hours and more leisure time .","translation":"اکثر مردم اکنون از ساعات کاری کوتاه تر و اوقات فراغت بیشتری لذت می برند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749299.mp3"},{"sentence":"Watching television is now the nation’s most popular leisure activity .","translation":"تماشای تلویزیون در حال حاضر محبوب ترین فعالیت اوقات فراغت کشور است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749303.mp3"},{"sentence":"The hotel offers various leisure facilities such as a swimming pool and sauna.","translation":"این هتل دارای امکانات تفریحی مختلفی مانند استخر و سونا می باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749307.mp3"},{"sentence":"The leisure industry (= the business of providing leisure activities ) is now an important part of the economy.","translation":"صنعت اوقات فراغت (= کسب و کار ارائه فعالیت های اوقات فراغت) اکنون بخش مهمی از اقتصاد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001749311.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
