('e72cd06e-913b-5b64-aeaf-331ed9090e61','e9361b2a-734c-5211-b687-b8ef519e0083',1,'document','سند','spoken & written','an official document giving you permission to own or do something for a period of time','[ countable ]','driving licence','مجوز، پروانه؛ گواهی (رانندگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a licence Café Metropole does not yet have a license to sell liquor.','hold a licence British English (= have a licence ) Police said that the man did not hold a firearms licence.','get/gain/obtain a licence New private pilots must fly for at least fifty hours before getting their licences.','apply for a licence A doctor who moves to another state must apply for a license to practice medicine there.','grant/issue a licence He was granted his flying instructor’s licence.','renew a licence The licence must be renewed yearly.','lose your licence The police caught him driving while drunk and he will now lose his licence.','a licence runs out ( also a licence expires formal ) (= it ends ) Her driver’s license had expired.','take away somebody’s licence ( also revoke somebody''s licence formal ) The doctor had his license revoked after he was found to be on drugs.','a driving licence British English , a driver''s license American English 80 percent of 18 year olds had a driver’s license.','a pilot’s licence She became the youngest woman to hold a pilot’s licence.','a television licence British English (= which allows you to use your television and pays for public television programmes ) Buying a television means you will need a television licence.','a marriage licence (= a licence that allows two people to marry each other ) We went to get a marriage licence.','a fishing/hunting licence (= a licence that allows you to fish/hunt ) He renewed his hunting license.','an import/export licence An export licence was issued in August last year.','a provisional licence British English (= a temporary driving licence before you get your full licence ) Learner drivers need to obtain a provisional licence.','a full licence (= one that is not temporary and has no restrictions ) They offer insurance cover for drivers over 25 and under 70 years of age with a full licence.','the licence holder British English (= the person who has a licence ) the licence holder of a public house','a licence fee (= money you have to pay to get a licence ) The BBC is funded by a licence fee which all television owners have to pay.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The dealers applied for an export licence.","translation":"دلالان برای صدور مجوز صادرات اقدام کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001458492.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was arrested for driving without a license .","translation":"او به دلیل رانندگی بدون گواهینامه دستگیر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972432.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Tennessee Valley Authority applied for a license to operate the facility.","translation":"اداره دره تنسی درخواست مجوز برای بهره برداری از این تاسیسات کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972438.mp3"},{"sentence":"The owner of land could grant a licence to cut and remove timber.","translation":"صاحب زمین می توانست مجوز قطع و برداشت چوب را بدهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972442.mp3"},{"sentence":"I forgot to renew my licence .","translation":"یادم رفت گواهینامه ام را تمدید کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972446.mp3"},{"sentence":"Persistent offenders face losing their licence .","translation":"متخلفان دائمی با از دست دادن مجوز خود مواجه می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972451.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
