ing licence before you get your full licence ) Learner drivers need to obtain a provisional licence.','a full licence (= one that is not temporary and has no restrictions ) They offer insurance cover for drivers over 25 and under 70 years of age with a full licence.','the licence holder British English (= the person who has a licence ) the licence holder of a public house','a licence fee (= money you have to pay to get a licence ) The BBC is funded by a licence fee which all television owners have to pay.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Guinness is brewed under licence in South Africa.","translation":"گینس تحت مجوز در آفریقای جنوبی دم می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001736963.mp3"},{"sentence":"a licence agreement","translation":"یک قرارداد مجوز","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001736967.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
