('2a0ca641-b8c4-50aa-a066-3a5c60fbbb68','77d8ae88-f7c8-5164-8654-f7d965cd6f48',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a combination of two or more different things, feelings , or types of people','[ countable ]',null,'مخلوط، ترکیب؛ آمیزه (حس)؛ خوراک ترکیبی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The town is a mixture of the old and the new.","translation":"شهر آمیخته ای از قدیم و جدید است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648144.mp3"},{"sentence":"the mixture of different people living in the city","translation":"ترکیبی از افراد مختلف ساکن در شهر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000203779.mp3"},{"sentence":"She felt a strange mixture of excitement and fear.","translation":"او مخلوط عجیبی از هیجان و ترس را احساس کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000203780.mp3"},{"sentence":"a mixture of emotions","translation":"مخلوطی از احساسات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648145.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('eee1cf46-064e-5634-bf18-40ec773b9626','77d8ae88-f7c8-5164-8654-f7d965cd6f48',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a liquid or other substance made by mixing several substances together , especially in cooking','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'مایع یا ماده دیگری که از مخلوط کردن چند ماده با هم به خصوص در پخت و پز ایجاد می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Fill the bread with a mixture of lettuce, tomatoes, and cucumbers.","translation":"نان را با مخلوطی از کاهو، گوجه فرنگی و خیار پر کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001761482.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pour the mixture into four small dishes.","translation":"مخلوط را در چهار ظرف کوچک بریزید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648148.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6acf8b90-e600-58ff-b77a-6520b4307b25','77d8ae88-f7c8-5164-8654-f7d965cd6f48',3,null,null,'technical','a combination of substances that are put together but do not mix with each other','[ countable ]',null,'ترکیبی از موادی که در کنار هم قرار می گیرند اما با یکدیگر مخلوط نمی شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e4743f55-6a44-518b-9727-506d048cc5cc','ee2ca885-0948-5c72-a143-662bd1d09e0c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to carefully watch and check a situation in order to see how it changes over a period of time',null,null,'پایش کردن، رصد کردن؛ مانیتور کردن (بیمار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Patients who are given the new drug will be asked to monitor their progress.","translation":"از بیمارانی که داروی جدید به آنها داده می شود خواسته می شود تا پیشرفت خود را تحت نظر داشته باشند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000206623.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government is monitoring the situation closely .","translation":"دولت از نزدیک اوضاع را زیر نظر دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000206624.mp3"},{"sentence":"The temperature is carefully monitored .","translation":"دما به دقت کنترل می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566772.mp3"},{"sentence":"We need a better system for monitoring what is going on.","translation":"ما به یک سیستم بهتر برای نظارت بر آنچه در جریان است نیاز داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566778.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('f986748b-dff5-564a-b3bd-d9665a42d886','ee2ca885-0948-5c72-a143-662bd1d09e0c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to secretly listen to other people’s telephone calls, foreign radio broadcasts etc',null,null,'گوش دادن مخفیانه به تماس های تلفنی دیگران، برنامه های رادیویی خارجی و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He suspected that his phone calls were being monitored.","translation":"او مشکوک بود که تماس های تلفنی او تحت نظارت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000206629.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('accaaedb-6343-551b-9dc7-754826ebdbd1','25ae7f0a-66e1-5710-9b41-c41a6f418a41',1,'screen','صفحه نمایش','spoken & written','a television or part of a computer with a screen , on which you can see pictures or information',null,null,'تلویزیون یا بخشی از یک کامپیوتر با صفحه نمایش که می توانید تصاویر یا اطلاعات را روی آن ببینید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She was staring at her computer monitor.","translation":"به مانیتور کامپیوترش خیره شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566782.mp3"},{"sentence":"We could watch what was happening on the TV monitor.","translation":"می‌توانستیم آنچه را که در حال رخ دادن است روی مانیتور تلویزیون تماشا کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001754881.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('79a14b32-720f-5d02-b24a-09e40b8c26ad','25ae7f0a-66e1-5710-9b41-c41a6f418a41',2,'piece of equipment for measuring','قطعه ای از تجهیزات برای اندازه گیری','spoken & written','a piece of equipment that measures and shows the level, speed , temperature etc of something',null,null,'قطعه ای از تجهیزات که سطح، سرعت، دما و غیره چیزی را اندازه گیری و نشان می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a heart monitor","translation":"یک مانیتور قلب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000207459.mp3"},{"sentence":"The noise monitor recorded 98 decibels.","translation":"مانیتور نویز 98 دسی بل ضبط کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566794.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('32400497-07ee-56d2-bdce-7ead89c712eb','25ae7f0a-66e1-5710-9b41-c41a6f418a41',3,'somebody who watches an activity','کسی که یک فعالیت را تماشا می کند','spoken & written','someone whose job is to watch an activity or a situation to see how it changes or develops , or to make sure that it is fair and legal',null,null,'کسی که وظیفه اش این است که یک فعالیت یا موقعیت را تماشا کند تا ببیند چگونه تغییر می کند یا توسعه می یابد یا مطمئن شود که منصفانه و قانونی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"UN monitors will remain in the country to supervise the elections.","translation":"ناظران سازمان ملل برای نظارت بر انتخابات در کشور خواهند ماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566800.mp3"},{"sentence":"The UN is sending peace monitors to the area.","translation":"سازمان ملل ناظران صلح را به منطقه می فرستد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566803.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6afcad1b-7174-5e23-81d6-789bfa66aabf','25ae7f0a-66e1-5710-9b41-c41a6f418a41',4,'child','کودک','spoken & written','a child who has been chosen to help a teacher in some way in class',null,null,'کودکی که برای کمک به معلم در کلاس انتخاب شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fe6be8ab-6378-5e57-8d92-42a173a1eabe','25ae7f0a-66e1-5710-9b41-c41a6f418a41',5,'somebody who listens to radio','کسی که به رادیو گوش می دهد','spoken & written','someone whose job is to listen to news or messages on a radio and report on them',null,null,'کسی که وظیفه اش گوش دادن به اخبار یا پیام های رادیویی و گزارش آنهاست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f35592da-c996-5c50-9d68-6c1901c03d1d','80165abe-d267-588a-bce6-6d6f94d0969a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the early part of the day, from when the sun rises until 12 o ’ clock in the middle of the day',null,null,'صبح، بامداد؛ صبح (شنب)؛ صبح (کودکی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Friday/Monday/Saturday etc morning I’ll see you on Monday morning.','tomorrow morning Can you have the report ready by tomorrow morning?','yesterday morning I haven’t seen her since yesterday morning.','this morning (= today in the morning ) What did you do this morning?','the next morning/the following morning His meeting was not until the next morning.','late morning By the time he woke, it was late morning.','the early morning A light frost covered the fields in the early morning.','a beautiful/fine/sunny morning Outside it was a beautiful morning.','a cold/frosty morning Porridge tastes good on a cold morning.','a summer/winter etc morning They set off on a beautiful spring morning.','the morning sun/light/mist the warmth of the morning sun','a morning coffee/run/swim (= that someone does, drinks etc in the morning ) She read the paper while drinking her morning coffee.','the morning paper/news (= that is published or broadcast in the morning ) The story was in all the morning papers.','the morning train/flight (= that leaves in the morning ) She took the morning flight back to London.','early in the morning He has to get up very early in the morning.','first thing in the morning (= at the beginning of the morning ) She set off first thing in the morning.','from morning till night (= all day – used for emphasis ) He works from morning till night.','in the small hours of the morning (= very early, before dawn ) I was woken up in the small hours of the morning by a strange sound.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I hated those cold winter mornings.","translation":"از آن صبح های سرد زمستانی متنفر بودم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534978.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m not feeling very well this morning.","translation":"امروز صبح حالم خیلی خوب نیست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001057.mp3"},{"sentence":"He stayed in bed late on Sunday morning.","translation":"او یکشنبه صبح تا دیروقت در رختخواب ماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001974448.mp3"},{"sentence":"She took the early morning train.","translation":"او سوار قطار صبح زود شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001058.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('fee0979f-0951-51bf-83c6-f008d41b9cc8','80165abe-d267-588a-bce6-6d6f94d0969a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the part of the day from 12 o’clock at night until 12 o’clock in the middle of the day',null,null,'بخشی از روز از ساعت 12 شب تا ساعت 12 وسط روز','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Friday/Monday/Saturday etc morning I’ll see you on Monday morning.','tomorrow morning Can you have the report ready by tomorrow morning?','yesterday morning I haven’t seen her since yesterday morning.','this morning (= today in the morning ) What did you do this morning?','the next morning/the following morning His meeting was not until the next morning.','late morning By the time he woke, it was late morning.','the early morning A light frost covered the fields in the early morning.','a beautiful/fine/sunny morning Outside it was a beautiful morning.','a cold/frosty morning Porridge tastes good on a cold morning.','a summer/winter etc morning They set off on a beautiful spring morning.','the morning sun/light/mist the warmth of the morning sun','a morning coffee/run/swim (= that someone does, drinks etc in the morning ) She read the paper while drinking her morning coffee.','the morning paper/news (= that is published or broadcast in the morning ) The story was in all the morning papers.','the morning train/flight (= that leaves in the morning ) She took the morning flight back to London.','early in the morning He has to get up very early in the morning.','first thing in the morning (= at the beginning of the morning ) She set off first thing in the morning.','from morning till night (= all day – used for emphasis ) He works from morning till night.','in the small hours of the morning (= very early, before dawn ) I was woken up in the small hours of the morning by a strange sound.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The phone rang at three in the morning.","translation":"تلفن ساعت سه صبح زنگ خورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000209916.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s four o’clock in the morning.","translation":"ساعت چهار صبح است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001534983.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('427bf25a-44ff-55aa-bd55-fc7706f9523c','80165abe-d267-588a-bce6-6d6f94d0969a',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in the morning','صبح، بامداد؛ صبح (شنب)؛ صبح (کودکی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['Friday/Monday/Saturday etc morning I’ll see you on Monday morning.','tomorrow morning Can you have the report ready by tomorrow morning?','yesterday morning I haven’t seen her since yesterday morning.','this morning (= today in the morning ) What did you do this morning?','the next morning/the following morning His meeting was not until the next morning.','late morning By the time he woke, it was late morning.','the early morning A light frost covered the fields in the early morning.','a beautiful/fine/sunny morning Outside it was a beautiful morning.','a cold/frosty morning Porridge tastes good on a cold morning.','a summer/winter etc morning They set off on a beautiful spring morning.','the morning sun/light/mist the warmth of the morning sun','a morning coffee/run/swim (= that someone does, drinks etc in the morning ) She read the paper while drinking her morning coffee.','the morning paper/news (= that is published or broadcast in the morning ) The story was in all the morning papers.','the morning train/flight (= that leaves in the morning ) She took the morning flight back to London.','early in the morning He has to get up very early in the morning.','first thing in the morning (= at the beginning of the morning ) She set off first thing in the morning.','from morning till night (= all day – used for emphasis ) He works from morning till night.','in the small hours of the morning (= very early, before dawn ) I was woken up in the small hours of the morning by a strange sound.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
