('601091c0-a7df-5fef-b195-29ba900cc0a4','d48859b5-ad56-54ff-9b9e-1806e5f5925e',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a shape used as a guide for making something, especially a thin piece of paper used when cutting material to make clothes',null,null,'شکلی که به عنوان راهنما برای ساختن چیزی استفاده می شود، به خصوص یک تکه کاغذ نازک که هنگام برش مواد برای ساخت لباس استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a pattern of behaviour It''s easy to get stuck in the same old pattern of behaviour.','a pattern of development Regular checks help to ensure that the child is following the normal pattern of development','the same/a similar pattern Each of the murders has followed a similar pattern.','a different pattern There are different patterns of social life in urban areas.','the basic pattern The basic pattern of her working day rarely changed.','the general pattern The general pattern of change has been one of upward mobility.','the normal/usual pattern As soon as she could, she resumed the normal pattern of her life.','a set/fixed pattern (= one that does not change ) These incidents followed a set pattern.','a weather pattern Rising global temperatures are affecting weather patterns.','a behaviour pattern He studied animal behaviour patterns.','a sleep pattern Disturbed sleep patterns may be a symptom of depression.','a speech pattern Computers are now able to produce acceptable speech patterns.','a spending pattern The bank’s computer can detect unusual spending patterns.','a pattern emerges (= can be seen when something is studied ) Although the numbers are small, a pattern began to emerge.','follow a pattern Her headaches did not seem to follow any particular pattern.','fit a pattern ( also conform to a pattern formal ) (= match a particular pattern ) Last week’s bombing fits this pattern.','establish a pattern You should try to establish a pattern of working that suits you.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a dress pattern","translation":"یک الگوی لباس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000373607.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('dcb905fc-32db-5e71-9113-15bb047f563e','d48859b5-ad56-54ff-9b9e-1806e5f5925e',5,null,null,'spoken & written','a small piece of cloth , paper etc that shows what a larger piece will look like',null,null,'یک تکه پارچه کوچک، کاغذ و غیره که نشان می دهد یک قطعه بزرگتر چگونه به نظر می رسد',array['sample']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a pattern of behaviour It''s easy to get stuck in the same old pattern of behaviour.','a pattern of development Regular checks help to ensure that the child is following the normal pattern of development','the same/a similar pattern Each of the murders has followed a similar pattern.','a different pattern There are different patterns of social life in urban areas.','the basic pattern The basic pattern of her working day rarely changed.','the general pattern The general pattern of change has been one of upward mobility.','the normal/usual pattern As soon as she could, she resumed the normal pattern of her life.','a set/fixed pattern (= one that does not change ) These incidents followed a set pattern.','a weather pattern Rising global temperatures are affecting weather patterns.','a behaviour pattern He studied animal behaviour patterns.','a sleep pattern Disturbed sleep patterns may be a symptom of depression.','a speech pattern Computers are now able to produce acceptable speech patterns.','a spending pattern The bank’s computer can detect unusual spending patterns.','a pattern emerges (= can be seen when something is studied ) Although the numbers are small, a pattern began to emerge.','follow a pattern Her headaches did not seem to follow any particular pattern.','fit a pattern ( also conform to a pattern formal ) (= match a particular pattern ) Last week’s bombing fits this pattern.','establish a pattern You should try to establish a pattern of working that suits you.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dd4b177e-22fe-55c6-a3bb-9e61e90f2213','0450f32d-8d4e-5fa1-97a9-93fa491e49e1',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be patterned on/after something',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e12f23b2-5a41-58a6-810f-23ed5c7b0062','0450f32d-8d4e-5fa1-97a9-93fa491e49e1',2,null,null,'literary','to form a pattern on something',null,null,'برای تشکیل الگوی چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Tiny white flowers patterned the ground like confetti.","translation":"گل‌های سفید ریز زمین را مانند کنفتی طرح‌ریزی کرده‌اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001589498.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8b6034ab-84f7-530a-b9c1-8027e483191f','3c3d4037-36e1-5fc3-8395-6a595683f15e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an amount of money that has been or must be paid','[ countable ]',null,'پرداخت، مبلغ پرداختی؛ اقساط (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make (a) payment He was supposed to make payments of $250 a month.','receive (a) payment You will receive a cash payment on your 65th birthday.','meet/keep up the payments (on something) (= be able to make regular payments ) He was having trouble meeting the interest payments.','fall behind on the payments ( also fall behind with the payments British English ) (= not make payments when you should ) I’d run up nearly £4,000 in debt, and was beginning to fall behind with the payments.','a monthly payment Home buyers have seen their monthly payments go up by more than 50 percent.','a cash payment (= a payment in cash ) He provided pills to athletes in return for cash payments.','a down payment (= a small payment for something you are buying, when you will pay the rest later ) We were able to put a down payment on an apartment.','an interest payment (= a payment of interest on a loan )','a mortgage payment (= a payment towards a loan on your house ) Your mortgage payments could fall if interest rates drop.','an interim payment (= a payment that is made before something is finished or settled ) It may be reasonable for the builder to ask for interim payments as the work progresses.','a bonus payment (= an additional payment because success has been achieved ) The team had made illegal bonus payments to players.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"You can make a payment in any bank.","translation":"می توانید در هر بانکی پرداخت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942397.mp3"},{"sentence":"They fell behind on their mortgage payments.","translation":"آنها از پرداخت وام مسکن عقب افتادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942423.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('eb3904b9-4113-508f-a50a-b257eb97ae28','3c3d4037-36e1-5fc3-8395-6a595683f15e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the act of paying for something','[ uncountable ]',null,'عمل پرداخت برای چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make (a) payment He was supposed to make payments of $250 a month.','receive (a) payment You will receive a cash payment on your 65th birthday.','meet/keep up the payments (on something) (= be able to make regular payments ) He was having trouble meeting the interest payments.','fall behind on the payments ( also fall behind with the payments British English ) (= not make payments when you should ) I’d run up nearly £4,000 in debt, and was beginning to fall behind with the payments.','a monthly payment Home buyers have seen their monthly payments go up by more than 50 percent.','a cash payment (= a payment in cash ) He provided pills to athletes in return for cash payments.','a down payment (= a small payment for something you are buying, when you will pay the rest later ) We were able to put a down payment on an apartment.','an interest payment (= a payment of interest on a loan )','a mortgage payment (= a payment towards a loan on your house ) Your mortgage payments could fall if interest rates drop.','an interim payment (= a payment that is made before something is finished or settled ) It may be reasonable for the builder to ask for interim payments as the work progresses.','a bonus payment (= an additional payment because success has been achieved ) The team had made illegal bonus payments to players.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are severe penalties for late payment of taxes.","translation":"جریمه های سنگینی برای تاخیر در پرداخت مالیات وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665624.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most hotels here accept payment in dollars.","translation":"اکثر هتل های اینجا پرداخت را به دلار می پذیرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665621.mp3"},{"sentence":"Payment can be made by cheque or credit card.","translation":"پرداخت را می توان با چک یا کارت اعتباری انجام داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665614.mp3"},{"sentence":"We do accept payment in instalments (= paying in small amounts over a period of time ) .","translation":"ما پرداخت را به صورت اقساط می پذیریم (= پرداخت در مقادیر کم در یک دوره زمانی).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000377652.mp3"},{"sentence":"She demanded payment in advance .","translation":"او پیشاپیش درخواست پرداخت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665628.mp3"},{"sentence":"cheques received in payment for goods supplied","translation":"چک های دریافتی در پرداخت کالای عرضه شده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665638.mp3"},{"sentence":"Any item can be reserved on payment of a deposit.","translation":"هر موردی را می توان با پرداخت بیعانه رزرو کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000377660.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('7daadea1-1d8a-5092-ad76-a48311388789','3c3d4037-36e1-5fc3-8395-6a595683f15e',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'payment in kind','پرداخت، مبلغ پرداختی؛ اقساط (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make (a) payment He was supposed to make payments of $250 a month.','receive (a) payment You will receive a cash payment on your 65th birthday.','meet/keep up the payments (on something) (= be able to make regular payments ) He was having trouble meeting the interest payments.','fall behind on the payments ( also fall behind with the payments British English ) (= not make payments when you should ) I’d run up nearly £4,000 in debt, and was beginning to fall behind with the payments.','a monthly payment Home buyers have seen their monthly payments go up by more than 50 percent.','a cash payment (= a payment in cash ) He provided pills to athletes in return for cash payments.','a down payment (= a small payment for something you are buying, when you will pay the rest later ) We were able to put a down payment on an apartment.','an interest payment (= a payment of interest on a loan )','a mortgage payment (= a payment towards a loan on your house ) Your mortgage payments could fall if interest rates drop.','an interim payment (= a payment that is made before something is finished or settled ) It may be reasonable for the builder to ask for interim payments as the work progresses.','a bonus payment (= an additional payment because success has been achieved ) The team had made illegal bonus payments to players.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8efc5621-d0f9-518d-a5d1-d4a1cbc45956','79a1a271-406e-58e7-92f7-5884e570c338',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a punishment for breaking a law , rule , or legal agreement',null,null,'جریمه، مجازات؛ ضربه (توپ)؛ جریمه (مالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a severe/stiff/heavy/tough/harsh penalty There were calls for stiffer penalties for killers of police officers.','the maximum penalty The maximum penalty for the offence is now three years’ imprisonment.','a financial penalty Parents who fail to prevent their children committing crimes are to face heavy financial penalties.','the death penalty (= the punishment of being killed ) If convicted, they face the death penalty.','a crime carries a penalty Murder carries a minimum penalty of 15 years in prison.','impose a penalty Severe penalties are imposed for election fraud.','face a penalty He faces a maximum penalty of 10 years’ imprisonment.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"No littering. Penalty $500.","translation":"بدون زباله جریمه 500 دلار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000347343.mp3"},{"sentence":"Withdrawing the money early will result in a 10% penalty.","translation":"برداشت زودهنگام پول 10 درصد جریمه خواهد داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559700.mp3"},{"sentence":"The penalty for a first offense is a fine.","translation":"مجازات اولین تخلف جریمه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000347346.mp3"},{"sentence":"Drug dealers face severe penalties.","translation":"فروشندگان مواد مخدر با مجازات های شدید روبرو هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559701.mp3"},{"sentence":"If he is convicted, he could receive the death penalty (= be killed as a punishment ) .","translation":"اگر مجرم شناخته شود، ممکن است مجازات اعدام (= قتل به عنوان مجازات) دریافت کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559702.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('ade6912e-6034-5357-a51c-943d4786c5b8','79a1a271-406e-58e7-92f7-5884e570c338',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something bad that happens to you because of something you have done or because of the situation you are in',null,null,'اتفاق بدی که به خاطر کاری که انجام داده اید یا به دلیل موقعیتی که در آن هستید برای شما اتفاق می افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"One of the penalties of being famous is the loss of privacy.","translation":"یکی از جریمه های معروف بودن از دست دادن حریم خصوصی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000347362.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you don’t do the job right, you will pay the penalty .","translation":"اگر کار را درست انجام ندهید، جریمه را پرداخت خواهید کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559707.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('0333c851-e550-59d8-957d-d9a5c53be770','79a1a271-406e-58e7-92f7-5884e570c338',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a disadvantage in sports given to a player or team for breaking a rule',null,null,'ضرری که در ورزش به یک بازیکن یا تیم داده می شود تا یک قانون را زیر پا بگذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Woodson received a penalty.","translation":"وودسون یک پنالتی دریافت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001559711.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('89be3044-8b97-51f8-b581-51cf30837530','79a1a271-406e-58e7-92f7-5884e570c338',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a chance to kick the ball or hit the puck into the goal in a game of football , rugby , or ice hockey , given because the other team has broken a rule',null,null,'در بازی فوتبال، راگبی یا هاکی روی یخ، فرصتی برای ضربه زدن به توپ یا ضربه زدن به توپ به دروازه، به این دلیل داده شده است که تیم مقابل قانون را زیر پا گذاشته است.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Townsend kicked a penalty (= in a rugby game ) in the last minute.","translation":"تاونسند در آخرین دقیقه یک پنالتی (= در بازی راگبی) زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001839779.mp3"},{"sentence":"Leeds were awarded a penalty.","translation":"لیدز پنالتی گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001839786.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c2b4cf99-ca37-5142-a826-9e0eea4a5311','fcf78554-ca39-5b8b-a6ee-1dc4d57b3591',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an amount of money paid regularly by the government or company to someone who does not work anymore, for example because they have reached the age when people stop working or because they are ill',null,null,'بازنشستگی، مستمری؛ مستمری (سازمان)؛ معاش (بازنشسته)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['get/receive a pension They receive the basic state pension.','draw your pension (= receive it ) He''s got another ten years before he draws his pension.','collect your pension (= receive it or go to get it ) She went to the post office every week to collect her pension.','pay into a pension (= pay money regularly so that you will have a pension later ) They have been unable to pay into a pension.','take out a pension (= make arrangements to have a pension later ) People were encouraged to take out private pensions.','an old age pension State old age pensions were introduced in 1908.','a retirement pension Many workers lost their retirement pensions when the fund collapsed.','a state pension British English , a public pension American English (= one that the government pays ) They argued that the state pension should rise in line with average earnings.','a company/occupational pension (= one that your employer pays ) I''ve been paying into the company pension scheme for 20 years.','a private/personal pension (= one that you arrange with a private pension company ) The percentage of the workforce with a private pension has declined.','pension contributions (= money that you pay into a pension ) You can make additional pension contributions.','pension provision (= when you pay money regularly so that you will have a pension later ) They can''t afford to make adequate pension provision for themselves.','pension age (= the age when you can get a pension ) Most men stayed in their jobs until pension age.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At what age can you start drawing your pension ?","translation":"از چه سنی می توانید بازنشستگی خود را شروع کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942153.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you are self-employed, you should think about taking out a private pension .","translation":"اگر خوداشتغال هستید، باید به فکر گرفتن حقوق بازنشستگی خصوصی باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942163.mp3"},{"sentence":"Many people find it hard to live on a basic state pension .","translation":"برای بسیاری از مردم زندگی با حقوق بازنشستگی دولتی دشوار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942159.mp3"},{"sentence":"She pays a quarter of her salary into a pension plan .","translation":"او یک چهارم حقوق خود را به برنامه بازنشستگی می پردازد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942169.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('ea898bfa-ba9c-558f-8fae-a90a9b9019f2','668ca188-d0f8-5c02-9f44-2e074a067e7b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone leave their job when they are old or ill , and pay them a pension',null,'pension somebody/something off','وادار کردن کسی در زمان پیری یا بیماری شغل خود را ترک کند و به او حقوق بازنشستگی بپردازد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Not everyone wants to be pensioned off at 65.","translation":"همه نمی خواهند در 65 سالگی بازنشسته شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000348374.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6b7595ff-cf93-5432-b197-352c226d6ac0','ce1659b5-0de4-5edb-bf9c-51e8a0c233d5',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a small cheap hotel in France and some other European countries',null,null,'یک هتل ارزان کوچک در فرانسه و برخی کشورهای اروپایی دیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0)
